three classes FoodResponse,FoodEntity,FoodRequest work together in your API:

Clients send data to create a new food item using the structure defined in FoodRequest.
Your API's controller layer receives this FoodRequest and likely passes it to the service layer.
The service layer might convert the FoodRequest into a FoodEntity to interact with the database. The imageUrl would be handled separately (e.g., after uploading an image to S3).
The FoodEntity is then saved to the MongoDB database.
When clients request food item data, the API retrieves FoodEntity objects from the database and converts them into FoodResponse objects to send back to the client.